diff --git a/packages/eslint-plugin/docs/rules/no-unguarded-get-range-at.md b/packages/eslint-plugin/docs/rules/no-unguarded-get-range-at.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000000..1dd2e3e3ec44b0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/eslint-plugin/docs/rules/no-unguarded-get-range-at.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Avoid unguarded getRangeAt (no-unguarded-get-range-at)
+
+Some browsers (e.g. Safari) will throw an error when `getRangeAt` is called and there are no ranges in the selection.
+
+## Rule details
+
+Example of **incorrect** code for this rule:
+
+```js
+window.getSelection().getRangeAt( 0 );
+```
+
+Example of **correct** code for this rule:
+
+```js
+const selection = window.getSelection();
+const range = selection.rangeCount ? selection.getRangeAt( 0 ) : null;
+```
